christoffel-symbol-lower-index-symmetry-.symmetry_origin:
Geometric Invariance. This symmetry is a direct consequence of defining the connection (the Christoffel symbol) from a metric tensor $g_{\mu
u}$ that is itself symmetric ($g_{\mu
u} = g_{
u\mu}$) and requiring the connection to be torsion-free. The torsion tensor is defined as $T^{\lambda}_{\mu
u} = \Gamma^{\lambda}_{\mu
u} - \Gamma^{\lambda}_{
u\mu}$. The torsion-free condition $T^{\lambda}_{\mu
u} = 0$ directly implies $\Gamma^{\lambda}_{\mu
u} = \Gamma^{\lambda}_{
u\mu}$.
